    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Instructions \n**Create a 'Manual Event Webhook'**\nhttps://developer.getadministrate.com/docs/core/Webhooks/02_setup.md\n1. Set the webhookTypeId: \"V2ViaG9va1R5cGU6bWFudWFsX2V2ZW50\"\n2. Set the name: \"Create Booking with Event as Interest\"\n3. Set the url to the n8n url that's provided when creating the Webhook node.\n4. Set the query to \"query test($objectid: ID!){ node(id: $objectid) { id ... on Event{ code type bookingAccount{id}price region{id}defaultTaxType{id}financialUnit{id}defaultPrice{amount financialUnit{id }}}}}\"\n\n\n**Update the entryStepId**\nUnder the Create Booking node and Private Create Booking node, update the entryStepId to your preference of Booking Step the Booking should be created in",
        "height": 448,
        "width": 416
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -512,
        -48
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "ac030a7a-09dc-4388-ac70-223513594791",
      "name": "Sticky Note3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What Does It Do?\nA Booking can be created directly from an Event, the Event will automatically be added as an Interest on the newly created Booking. \n\nUnder the 'Automator' menu on an Event, you will see \"Create Booking with Event as Interest\" option.\n\nThe Public Event needs to meet this criteria:\n- Active\n- Start Date in the future\n- Default Price Level set\n\n_Please note: Training Tokens cannot be set as a Default Price_\n\n\nThe Private Event needs to meet this criteria:\n- Active \n- Start Date in the future\n- Price set\n\n_Please note: Training Tokens cannot be set as a Price_",
        "height": 512,
        "width": 416,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -960,
        -48
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "714f2e53-de73-4f12-86da-d58938bf7037",
      "name": "Sticky Note4"
    },
